       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for sertraline in adults, which is 200 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI effects, and agitation. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nPlease check which of these fits:\n\n1. **Dose typo:** you may have meant 200 mg, 100 mg, or 40 mg. Usual dosing starts at 25\u201350 mg daily and titrates in 25\u201350 mg steps at intervals of at least a week, up to 200 mg.\n2. **Intentional supratherapeutic dose:** if so, tell me the clinical rationale, such as a specialist recommendation or a documented plan. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably want to verify it.\n3. **Other drug or unit mix-up:** for example, a different medication or a different intended frequency.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
